✅ Fitness Function:
This function calculates how good an antibody (solution) is.

The input antibody is a list of 0s and 1s (e.g., [1, 0, 1, 1]).

It adds up all the 1s. A higher number of 1s means a better solution.

🧬 Generate a Random Antibody (Binary String):
This function creates a random binary string (an antibody).

size specifies how long the string is.

It randomly picks 0 or 1 for each position in the list.

🧪 Generate Initial Population:
This function creates the first group of antibodies (initial guesses).

pop_size is how many antibodies to create.

Each antibody is generated randomly using the function above.

🥇 Select the Best Antibodies (Based on Fitness):
This function picks the best antibodies based on how many 1s they have.

It sorts all the antibodies by fitness.

Then it keeps only the top few (usually the top 50%).

🧫 Clone the Selected Antibodies:
This function makes copies (clones) of the best antibodies.

Better antibodies are cloned more times.

These clones will later be mutated to try and improve them.

🔁 Hypermutation: Apply Small Mutations to Clones:
This function introduces small changes (mutations) in each clone.

Each bit (0 or 1) has a chance to flip (from 0 to 1 or 1 to 0).

These mutations allow the algorithm to explore new possibilities.

🔄 Replace Worst Antibodies with Random New Ones:
This function removes the worst antibodies (poor solutions).

It replaces them with new random antibodies.

This keeps the population diverse and prevents getting stuck.

🔍 Clonal Selection Algorithm: (Main Process)
This function runs the full optimization loop.

Parameters:

pop_size: Number of antibodies in the population.

size: Length of each antibody.

generations: How many times to repeat the process.

clone_factor: How many clones to make.

mutation_rate: Chance of flipping each bit.

🔄 For each generation:
Select the top 50% of antibodies.

Clone the selected ones based on clone factor.

Mutate the clones slightly (hypermutation).

Add mutated clones to the current population.

Select the best antibodies from the expanded population.

Replace the worst ones with new random ones (bottom 20%).

Print the best antibody and its fitness for the current generation.

🏁 Final Result:
After all generations, it returns the best antibody (solution with the most 1s).



